pan></a><button aria-controls="primary-nav" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open navigation menu" class="mobile-menu" type="button">Menu</button><nav aria-label="Main navigation" class="nav" id="primary-nav"><a href="../../en/index.html">Overview</a><a href="../../en/projects/index.html">Projects</a><a href="../../en/roadmap/index.html">Roadmap</a><a href="../../en/contact/index.html">Contact</a></nav><nav aria-label="Language / Taal" class="language-switch"><a data-language-switch="nl" href="../../projects/ohsint-investigation.html" lang="nl">NL</a><a aria-current="true" aria-label="Current language: English" data-language-switch="en" href="../../en/projects/ohsint-investigation.html">EN</a></nav><div class="theme-switch" role="group" aria-label="Color theme"><button type="button" class="theme-choice" data-theme-select="dark" aria-pressed="true" aria-label="Dark theme" title="Dark theme"><span aria-hidden="true">☾</span></button><button type="button" class="theme-choice" data-theme-select="light" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Light theme" title="Light theme"><span aria-hidden="true">☼</span></button></div><a aria-label="About Jeroen and contact" class="profile-link" href="../../en/contact/index.html"><img alt="" height="40" src="../../assets/jeroen-portrait.webp" width="40"/><span>Jeroen</span></a></div></div></div><main id="main"><div class="shell"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="../../en/projects/index.html">← All cases</a><span>/</span><span>CTFs</span></div><header class="page-header"><div class="eyebrow">Security case · CTF investigation</div><h1>OhSINT Investigation</h1><p>A guided open-source intelligence challenge examining what image metadata and publicly available information can reveal.</p></header><div class="dossier-meta"><span class="pill completed">Completed</span><span>25 okt 2026</span><span>Evidence-based case — no simulated results</span></div><div class="dossier-layout"><div class="dossier-content"><img alt="" class="dossier-art" decoding="async" height="900" loading="eager" src="../../assets/osint-map-hd.svg" width="1600"/><p class="dossier-kicker">A guided open-source intelligence challenge examining what image metadata and publicly available information can reveal.</p><section><h2>Research question</h2><p>What can metadata and open sources disclose about a person or location, and how reliable is each individual clue?</p></section><section><h2>Method and tools</h2><ul><li>Inspected the challenge image using Windows, PowerShell and ExifTool.</li><li>Distinguished EXIF- and XMP-related fields from interpretation and external open-source clues.</li><li>Used the gathered clues to complete the seven TryHackMe questions with coaching.</li></ul><p class="status-evidence">Tools: Windows · PowerShell · ExifTool · Public sources</p></section><section><h2>Observations and evidence</h2><p>All 7/7 questions were completed with guidance. The Wi-Fi SSID clue was supplied by the coach and was not independently verified.</p></section><section><h2>Limitations</h2><p>Completing the challenge does not establish independent OSINT proficiency. Attribution requires checkable, independent supporting sources.</p></section><section><h2>What I learned</h2><p>Strip unnecessary location or device metadata from published images. Record provenance and uncertainty for each OSINT observation.</p></section><section><h2>Next verification step</h2><p>Repeat a comparable investigation independently and document which sources were actually verified.</p></section></div><aside class="dossier-aside"><h2>Evidence status</h2><span class="pill completed">Completed</span><p>All 7/7 questions were completed with guidance. The Wi-Fi SSID clue was supplied by the coach and was not independently verified.</p><div class="divider"></div><h3>Next checkpoint</h3><p>Repeat a comparable investigation independently and document which sources were actually verified.</p></aside></div></div></main><noscript><p class="shell">All content is available without JavaScript. JavaScript enables the interactive search and filters.</p></noscript><footer id="footer"><div class="shell footer"><span>© Jeroen · Security Engineering · Manually reviewed public portfolio content</span><div><a href="../methodology/index.html">Methodology &amp; evidence</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="../../en/roadmap/index.html">Learning roadmap</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="../../en/contact/index.html">Contact</a></div></div></footer><script defer="" src="../../assets/dashboard.js"></script></body></html>